<!--
  The simple F-4C's engine, a J79, for JSBSim v1.3.3's turbine. FSG's own file: new in FSG, milestone 3
  re-planned (docs/milestones/3-replan.md, pull request 3). JSBSim finds it in the aircraft's own Engines
  folder before it looks in its shared engine folder.

  The two ratings are the flight manual's, as the data-built F-4C's engine has them (T.O. 1F-4C-1, section I:
  "the J79-15 engine is rated at 10,900 pounds thrust at Mil power, while Max power is rated at 17,000"):
  both engines together 21,800 and 34,000 lb, Wings' card's two thrust numbers.

  How thrust changes with speed and height is Wings' plain rule (135crewdog/wings, src/sim/engine.js,
  commit 6d689b7): it thins with the air (the density ratio to the power 0.7); MIL thrust sags a little
  with speed and recovers (1 - 0.2 M + 0.25 M squared); afterburner thrust climbs with it (1 + 0.35 M
  squared); idle is 5% of MIL. tools/simple-thrust.mjs makes the three tables from the rule and says exactly
  how; they are written there and nowhere by hand, and tests/simple-f4c.test.js holds this file to the tool.
  (The data-built jet's engine is JSBSim's generic J79 anchored to NASA CR-2144's drag: more thrust up
  high at Mach 2, less at sea level. This rule alone meets both of this airplane's top speeds.)

  The rest is the data-built engine's (aircraft/f4c/Engines/J79-GE-15.xml), as it is there: the afterburner
  is JSBSim's method 2 (the throttle the engine is given runs 0 to 1 from idle to MIL and 1 to 2 through
  the afterburner; the aircraft file's throttle system gives it that), idle at 53%, no bypass, and JSBSim's
  own spool-up. The fuel figures change nothing while the game freezes the fuel.
-->
<turbine_engine name="J79">
  <milthrust>   10900.0 </milthrust>
  <maxthrust>   17000.0 </maxthrust>
  <bypassratio>     0.0 </bypassratio>
  <tsfc>            0.95 </tsfc>
  <atsfc>           1.90 </atsfc>
  <idlen1>          0.0 </idlen1>
  <idlen2>         53.0 </idlen2>
  <maxn1>         100.0 </maxn1>
  <maxn2>         100.0 </maxn2>
  <augmented>         1 </augmented>
  <augmethod>         2 </augmethod>
  <injected>          0 </injected>

